  "timing_definition": "Target-app acknowledged clicks: elapsed from first to last action within one burst. Preparation and launch latency are separate. Native pass tolerance was <200ms for the requested ~100ms burst; actual tested background spans were 48-53ms and foreground 27ms.",
  "delivery": "Current-Space background bursts use exact-window NSEvent/CGEvent delivery with a dynamically resolved CGEventSetWindowLocation compatibility symbol. This CoreGraphics symbol is not public API. When unavailable, Accessibility delivery remains available; fast events mode reports unsupported rather than claiming a successful burst. Inactive-Space Accessibility presses and app-specific handlers can run slower.",
  "initial_failures_and_fixes": [
    "Accessibility button presses serialized native animations, exceeding the burst target. Current-Space bursts use fast balanced window-routed events.",
    "Raw pid-routed CG events arrived with window number zero. NSEvent creation supplies the explicit target window number.",
    "Global and window-local event locations must be populated separately on multiple displays. A native probe confirmed the optional CoreGraphics bridge, followed by installed-app verification.",
    "Switching an already-used multi-point picker to one-shot mode ignored the next point because the previous capture count remained nonzero. Arming one-shot resets its count; re-pick was verified by changed coordinates and resulting click order.",
    "The automated Escape key did not finish the HID picker reliably; native QA now uses Finish directly."
  ],
  "cleanup": "Temporary fixture apps quit; only Repeat settings changed by testing restored; no QA macros created; no clipboard contents read or modified."
}
